            {
                "entry_id": "cb18c51c-fa16-31a5-8a5e-b1536478aa9a",
                "word": "warder",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1098607d-dea0-4859-ad67-051cd6b8d8fe",
                        "entry_id": "cb18c51c-fa16-31a5-8a5e-b1536478aa9a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "warders"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "17fd6822-e8c3-3121-be5c-03fd1b6bff2c",
                        "entry_id": "cb18c51c-fa16-31a5-8a5e-b1536478aa9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A guard, especially in a prison."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e09e7e8a-5148-40aa-8de6-efcb4df69e02",
                                "sense_id": "17fd6822-e8c3-3121-be5c-03fd1b6bff2c",
                                "text": "Kent. Mortimer, ’tis I.\nBut hath thy portion wrought so happily?\nYounger Mortimer. It hath, my lord: the warders all asleep,\nI thank them, gave me leave to pass in peace."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62323973-c537-4194-9359-85fef0f13f8d",
                                "sense_id": "17fd6822-e8c3-3121-be5c-03fd1b6bff2c",
                                "text": "Above the gloomy portal arch, / Timing his footsteps to a march, / The warder kept his guard, / Low humming, as he paced along, / Some ancient Border gathering song."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b2e8384-25c6-4dcf-8adb-3aa993ee1d9c",
                                "sense_id": "17fd6822-e8c3-3121-be5c-03fd1b6bff2c",
                                "text": "So the guards carried him to the jail, thinking to lay him by the heels there for the night; but, when the warders saw his beauty and loveliness, they could not find it in their hearts to imprison him: they made him sit with them without the walls; and, when food came to them, he ate with them what sufficed him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "391f8c48-5b74-4297-bb32-163c0618cf95",
                                "sense_id": "17fd6822-e8c3-3121-be5c-03fd1b6bff2c",
                                "text": "Nobody else spoke, but they noticed the long stripes on Okonkwo’s back where the warder’s whip had cut into his flesh."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fc061ef0-efe8-325c-9a4b-bd32b40ee9b0",
                        "entry_id": "cb18c51c-fa16-31a5-8a5e-b1536478aa9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who or that which wards or repels."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31245e87-a8c8-4b65-bd5b-8286565618a1",
                                "sense_id": "fc061ef0-efe8-325c-9a4b-bd32b40ee9b0",
                                "text": "The conspicuous position thus accorded to the cat as a warder-off of evil fortune seems oddly paralleled, though not imitated, by the place accorded to the same animal in popular European folklore."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
